    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d34-a1-a4">

                <pb facs="0086" n="76" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg76"/>

                <head>Mr. John S. Seward to Messrs. Stringer, Pembroke &amp; Co.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Blackwell Iron Works,</hi><hi
                                rendition="#italic"> London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-10-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 3, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen:</hi> I will undertake to supply you with
                    marine screw engines for line-of-battle ships or rams, from 200 horse-power to
                    400 horse-power, for the sum of forty-eight pounds ten shillings per hundred
                    pounds, to be made of the <pb facs="0087" n="77" xml:id="pg77"/> best material
                    and workmanship; all the pipes to be copper; engine bearings moving in the best
                    gun metal, or white metal if approved, to be furnished to the entire
                    satisfaction of any person the mercantile marine company or yourselves may
                    appoint; and I also agree to make the engines from plans and specifications to
                    be sent home from the confederate government’s engineer, and to be finished in
                    six to eight months from date of order. I also agree to send out men, if
                    required, to place the engines in the respective ships, at the confederate
                    government’s expense.</p>
                <p>I am, gentlemen, yours truly,</p>
                <p rendition="#right">JNO. S. SEWARD.</p>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Messrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stringer, Pembroke</hi> &amp; Co., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Austin Friars.</hi></p>
                    <p>Original found on board the prize steamer Cornubia.</p>
                </postscript>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. H. DANA, <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jr</hi>., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Attorney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
